---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Projects · Terraform Drift Platform" description="Details for the Terraform Drift Detection & Auto-Remediation Platform.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="pill">Infrastructure Platform</div>
    <h1>Terraform Drift Detection & Auto-Remediation Platform</h1>
    <p class="hero-subtitle">
      A production-style platform that detects when live AWS infrastructure diverges from
      Terraform state, classifies severity with a policy engine, records an audit trail, and
      supports approval-based remediation via GitHub workflows.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Project Summary</h2>
    <p>
      The platform runs Terraform plans in refresh-only mode across multiple AWS accounts, parses
      JSON plans into typed models, and applies YAML-driven policies to assign severity and
      recommended actions. It writes compact audit records to DynamoDB, full JSON reports to S3,
      and sends structured notifications via SNS. Optional integration with GitHub Issues and
      Actions adds a human approval layer for remediation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Tech Stack</h2>
    <p>
      Terraform · Python 3.11 · AWS (DynamoDB, S3, SNS, IAM, Lambda) · GitHub Actions · YAML policy engine
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Architecture Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Scheduled drift scans run a Terraform plan with <code>-refresh-only -detailed-exitcode</code>.
      When drift is detected, a JSON plan is generated and parsed into normalized drift items. A
      policy engine classifies each change, and the result is persisted and published for
      downstream consumers like chat, incident tools, or approval workflows.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Documentation</h2>
    <p>These links point directly into the project documentation within this repository.</p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a href="../projects/terraform-drift-platform/README.md">
        <button class="btn-primary" type="button">Project README</button>
      </a>
      <a href="../projects/terraform-drift-platform/docs/architecture.md">
        <button class="btn-ghost" type="button">Architecture</button>
      </a>
      <a href="../projects/terraform-drift-platform/docs/runbook.md">
        <button class="btn-ghost" type="button">Runbook</button>
      </a>
      <a href="../projects/terraform-drift-platform/docs/threat_model.md">
        <button class="btn-ghost" type="button">Threat Model</button>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

